WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.100
What does a receptor do before its hormone arrives?

2
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.660
The family has two answers.

3
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.000
The first is a chaperone.

4
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.140
The glucocorticoid and androgen receptors wait mostly in the cytoplasm, held by

5
00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.440
chaperones built around Hsp90.

6
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.280
A chaperone is a protein that helps other proteins hold their shape.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.640
Here it keeps the pocket ready for hormone, and keeps the receptor off DNA.

8
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.860
When hormone binds, the receptor is released and moves into the nucleus.

9
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:40.820
There it pairs with a second copy of itself and binds its response elements.

10
00:00:41.733 --> 00:00:44.673
The second answer is to wait on the DNA.

11
00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:51.313
The receptors for thyroid hormone, retinoic acid and vitamin D stay in the nucleus,

12
00:00:51.713 --> 00:00:53.613
and so do the PPAR receptors.

13
00:00:54.393 --> 00:00:59.493
They bind DNA paired with a partner from the same family called RXR.

14
00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.473
Their two half sites point the same way.

15
00:01:02.993 --> 00:01:09.193
The gap between them helps decide which pair fits: one base for PPAR, three for

16
00:01:09.193 --> 00:01:13.833
vitamin D, four for thyroid hormone, five for retinoic acid.

17
00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:20.477
Without hormone, the thyroid hormone and retinoic acid receptors hold

18
00:01:20.477 --> 00:01:23.617
co-repressors, proteins that keep the gene off.

19
00:01:24.577 --> 00:01:29.897
Hormone releases the co-repressor and brings in its place a co-activator, a

20
00:01:29.897 --> 00:01:31.997
protein that helps switch the gene on.

21
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:36.830
An empty receptor of this kind is an active off.

22
00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:43.570
A gene carrying an empty thyroid hormone receptor is quieter than the same gene with

23
00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:44.990
no receptor at all.

24
00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:49.890
So a receptor can wait off the DNA, or wait on it.
